Acoustic Connect for Cordova

New Features

- `PushEnabled` in `ConnectConfig.json` — the master switch of push. `true` by
  default (push has always been on in this plugin, so existing apps keep it;
  the Capacitor plugin's `pushEnabled` is off by default). `false` builds an
  analytics-only app: Android takes the `connect` artifact with no Firebase, iOS
  enables the SDK without push and adds no `ConnectNSE`/`ConnectNCE` extensions,
  no App Group or `aps-environment` entitlement and no `remote-notification`
  background mode (a plugin or `config.xml` that declares it keeps it). The
  `push.*` calls then reject with `ACOUSTIC_PUSH_DISABLED`

Fixes

- iOS: the hook that rewrites the Podfile kept only the Connect pod and dropped
  the pods that the app's other plugins declare. It now keeps them, and restores
  the ones an earlier run lost from `pods.json`


Known Issues

- Rich push cannot be end-to-end tested on the iOS Simulator — simulators don't display large icon.
- Clicks and typing inside the page are not captured automatically — call
  `logClickEvent`/`logTextChangeEvent` yourself. They are sent as custom events
- Native layout masking rules do not mask text inside the WebView; use
  `ScreenCaptureEnabled: false` to keep page content out of captures
- `layoutConfigAndroid` replaces the Android SDK's whole layout config; the
  effect of layout rules on Android has not been verified
- On Android the SDK drops a screen view whose screen name is still queued, so
  `logScreenViewContextUnload` for the screen just loaded rejects with
  `ACOUSTIC_INTERNAL_ERROR`; unload the previous screen instead
- `logCustomEvent` values are nested under `data.value` on iOS but flat on
  Android, and a `logSignal` payload under `signal.data.value` on iOS but at the
  root of `signal` on Android; `logSignal` drops a top-level number on Android
  SDKs before 11.0.24-beta (the default is 11.1.17, which sends it)
- On iOS `logExceptionEvent` reports `stackTrace: (null)` and carries the stack
  text in `data.stacktrace`

Our environment for this release:

- Xcode 26.2
- MacOS 26.0.1
- iOS 15.1 to 26.x
- Android minSdk 26, SDK 36
